DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260424T123000
SUMMARY:Ledford/Sleepy Gap/Powhatan Loop: 6.5 mi.\, 1\,100 ft. elev.
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\n**[RSVP opens Sunday\, April 19th\
 , 8:00 pm]**\n\nWith so many trail segments cobbled together\, this is pra
 ctically a grand tour of the Bent Creek area! We'll start at the Ledford B
 ranch parking lot and cover parts of Bent Creek Gap Rd.\, Explorer Loop Tr
 ail\, Sleepy Gap Trail\, Shut-in Trail\, Deerfield Connector\, Small Creek
  Trail\, Homestead Trail\, Hard Times Rd.\, and Deer Lake Lodge Trail. (Th
 ere are a few other unnamed segments as well.) Total distance is around 6.
 5 miles with an elevation gain of just under 1\,100'. We'll do a moderate 
 pace of around 2.4 mph. It's not an easy hike for many of us. I'd give it 
 a 4 out of 10\, while many of my other hikes are in the 2 - 3.5 range with
  half the elevation gain.\n\nWear sensible hiking footwear\, and bring an 
 ample water supply. Around 2/3 of the way through\, we'll find a spot for 
 a short snack break.\n\n***Dog Policy:*** Dogs are extremely welcome but m
 ust be leashed.\n\n***Guest Policy:*** If you'd like to bring a guest\, th
 ey should join the Asheville Hiking Group and sign up for the hike on thei
 r own. Alternatively\, contact me in advance and ask if it's okay to bring
  a "+1" after you've made it onto the "Going" list. Depending on timing an
 d demand\, I MAY be able to add your guest.\n\n**MEET-UP TIME AND PLACE**\
 nPlease arrive at the Ledford Branch parking lot a few minutes early for s
 ign-in and introductions. It may be busy\, so leave some extra time in cas
 e you need to park along the access road and walk to the lot. We'll hit th
 e trail a.s.a.p. after 9:30 AM.\n\n**DIRECTIONS**\nFrom Exit 33 on I-26\,\
 nHead south on Brevard Rd. (Rt. 191) for 2 miles\nRight at the lights on B
 ent Creek Ranch Rd.\nAfter .3 miles bear left onto Wesley Branch Rd.\nGo a
 bout 2 miles\, past Rice Pinnacle and Hard Times Trailheads\nBear right at
  the fork & the sign for Ledford Branch Trailhead.\nGo around 500' to the 
 parking lot on the right.\n\n**[Google Maps link](https://maps.app.goo.gl/
 HjbbgfJryKjeHLJ4A)**\n\n**COURTESY TO WAIT-LISTERS (Please abide!)**\nOnly
  sign up if you \\*TRULY\\* plan to come. If you must cancel\, please chan
 ge your status to "Not Going" as soon as possible so wait-listers will hav
 e sufficient notice. And please please PLEASE don't be a no-show.\nIf you'
 re on the waiting list\, keep checking the evening before. Despite what I 
 wrote above\, we always get last-minute dropouts.\n\n**WEATHER**\nI'll mon
 itor National Weather Service forecasts for the hike area and email cancel
 lation messages by 7:30 AM if the forecast is for more than a 50% chance o
 f precipitation.\n\n**QUESTIONS?**\nIf you have any questions\, message me
  through MeetUp until 8:00 AM the day of. Cell reception may be sketchy on
  the trail\, but you can try to text or call me up to the start of the hik
 e: (803) 767-3094.\n\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\
 \-\\-\\-\n**LEGALESE**\nThis Asheville Hiking Group event involves hiking 
 and\, possibly\, transportation to and from the meetup site. Participants 
 are responsible for their own safety and\, by joining a hike\, affirm that
  they have the appropriate skills\, physical conditioning\, equipment\, an
 d supplies. Hiking may involve risks to oneself and property. Neither your
  hike organizer nor Asheville Hiking Group can eliminate all risks or be r
 esponsible for your well-being. Participants assume full responsibility fo
 r any injuries\, damages\, or losses.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/ashevillehikinggroup/events/314363474
 /
