DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260502T093000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260502T134500
SUMMARY:Scenic AVL Wildcard - Hendersonville - With AVL Camino Society
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\n**Overview:** This hike is offered
  as a monthly training hike with the WNC Asheville Chapter of the American
  Society of Pilgrims on the Camino. The route has been announced on the WN
 C Camino Group [Facebook Group Page](https://www.facebook.com/groups/AVLCa
 mino/announcements).\n\nThis route starts with a five mile loop\, a coffee
  break\, and a figure eight. We will stop at Southern Streams coffee to ch
 at about Camino preparation and the experience of walking the different ro
 utes\, including the Frances\, the Norte\, and the Portuguese. If you are 
 unfamiliar with the Camino\, here are a few links to learn more:\n\n*[Amer
 ican Pilgrims on the Camino](https://americanpilgrims.org/iwpmap_directory
 /western-north-carolina/)\n- [Stingy Nomads Camino](https://stingynomads.c
 om/camino-de-santiago-walking-guide/)\n*[Gronze Camino Planner](https://ww
 w.gronze.com/)\n\n**Distance:** This hike is made up of three sections\, a
 ll crossing the Ecusta trail. You can join and hike as much or as little a
 s you want 5 miles\, 7.5 or 10.5) For those who are just starting their tr
 aining\, come out and do the first or second half!\n\n***9:30am **- Meet a
 t First Congregational Church\, 1735 5th Ave W\, Hendersonville\, NC 2873\
 n*** First section is a five mile loop. **There is a short but steep climb
  up to Davis Mountain Road\, with a short stretch along a gravel road. Pac
 e will be 3.0 mph. The loop ends at Southern Streams coffee house\, which 
 is across from the church where we start.\n\n*** 11:00 am **- Southern Str
 eams Coffee house\, near FCC church. 30 minute coffee break and camino cha
 t. (if you want to sleep in\, meet us here at 11 ish)\n\n***Second Section
 : **Starting at about 11:30 am from Southern Streams coffee\, continue thr
 ough lower Laurel Park. For those who want to exit\, you can return to the
  church on the Ecusta Trail for a total of about 7 miles.\n\n*** Last Sect
 ion: **To downtown and St. James Church\, returning via Ecusta Trail. 10.5
  miles total distance. We plan to arrive at the church around 1:15 pm.\n\n
 **Elevation Gain: **800 ft total if you do the full 10.5.\n**Pace: **3.0-3
 .2 mph\n**Surface: **Road\, with short stretch on gravel road.\n**Rating: 
 **Strenuous for distance\, if you do the whole thing.\n**Features:**\n*Nei
 ghborhood charm\, last of the spring color\, Hendersonville downtown\, St 
 James church.\n*No bears. There may be geese or ducks on Rhododendron lake
 .\n\n**Cautions: **There are a few stretches on busy roads where we will n
 eed to walk single file.\n\n**Full Route: **[Laurel Park Loop](https://www
 .alltrails.com/explore/map/laurel-park-loop-improved-3937230?u=i&sh=ifwm3x
 )\n\n**Parking: **We are meeting at the First Congregational Church. Pleas
 e carpool if possible.\n\n**Gear: **2L water\, snacks\, cash for coffee at
  Southern Streams.\n**Dogs: **On leash the entire time.\n**After Event: **
 Some of us will go to [ El Sol y La Luna\, ](https://maps.app.goo.gl/pfvgk
 MsJztNXAANi9)Cali-Mex\, after the hike.\n\n**Scenic Asheville Series: **Th
 is hike counts as a Wildcard substitute on my Scenic Asheville Series. The
 re are 9 [hikes](https://docs.google.com/document/d/11ewlUM9OV8I4npc1cNNsS
 YOnXI0QPw2isAleXdFzEbI/edit?usp=drivesdk) in the series\; hike them all an
 d receive an [attractive badge](https://docs.google.com/drawings/d/1goXUXf
 zUBqhB4_UeCxodlk4ZPeCCgqZrWK2EUJvk_vI/edit) for your backpack. Check your 
 status [HERE](https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1XUm-X1_OhxKIi8JU5rhj
 sW37cAl4yYx8yB_NEjjI5Lk/edit?gid=0#gid=0).\n\n**On-Time Departure**\nWe wi
 ll start by walking the labyrinth at the First Congregational Church\, so 
 this is a pretty relaxed start.\n\n- Please change your RSVP as soon as yo
 u know you can't make it.\n*If you have questions\, call the hike leader (
 Gracen) at 828-290-0886.\n\n**Guests:** For this hike\, there are no guest
  restrictions. Bring them with you.\n\n**Disclaimer and Release of Liabili
 ty:**\nThis activity involves hiking on city streets that may have traffic
  and/or hiking on natural surfaces. Participants are responsible for their
  safety on streets and trails. The organizer of this trip is a volunteer a
 nd not a professional guide. The function of the organizer is only to orga
 nize this trip. If you sign up or participate in this event you acknowledg
 e that you freely and voluntarily agree to assume all risks of injuries\, 
 illnesses\, and damages arising from\, as a result of\, and associated wit
 h this event. You are responsible for any guests\, dogs or other companion
 s you bring with you. In addition\, you acknowledge that you agree to the 
 Meetup terms: [https://www.meetup.com/terms](https://www.meetup.com/terms)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/ashevillehikinggroup/events/314367727
 /
